# `loginproviders.sh`

```bash
#!/bin/bash

# ==========================================================
# Music Login Provider Launcher
# macOS
#
# Supports:
#   1. Google
#   2. Yahoo
#   3. Apple
#
# Credentials are entered directly on the provider's
# official website. This script never stores passwords.
# ==========================================================

echo ""
echo "======================================"
echo "       MUSIC ACCOUNT SIGN-IN"
echo "======================================"
echo ""
echo "1) Google"
echo "2) Yahoo"
echo "3) Apple"
echo "4) Exit"
echo ""

read -p "Choose a sign-in provider: " choice

case "$choice" in

    1)
        echo "Opening Google sign-in..."
        open "https://accounts.google.com/"
        ;;

    2)
        echo "Opening Yahoo sign-in..."
        open "https://login.yahoo.com/"
        ;;

    3)
        echo "Opening Apple sign-in..."
        open "https://account.apple.com/"
        ;;

    4)
        echo "Exiting."
        exit 0
        ;;

    *)
        echo "Invalid choice."
        exit 1
        ;;

esac

echo ""
echo "Sign in using the official provider page."
echo "Your password is not handled by this script."
echo ""
```

### Menu

```text
MUSIC ACCOUNT SIGN-IN

1) Google
2) Yahoo
3) Apple
4) Exit
```

This is a **launcher**, not a credential collector. Google, Yahoo, and Apple handle the actual authentication themselves.
